  "selectedReplayRule": "Current required authorization precedes replay; exact authorized retries resolve the original accepted result using the selected logical identity and immutable actor/intent/source binding. Fresh mutable feasibility, clock selection and body preparation cannot replace that original result. Expected revision is concurrency precondition, not a new identity.",
  "productRules": [
    {
      "id": "D01-02",
      "doc": "m0-d01-program-targets.md",
      "rule": "Program target dates are optional (nullable) values that carry author and revision attribution; a target date is never promoted to an auditor-confirmed date by passage of time, status display, or an imported note."
    },
    {
      "id": "D01-04",
      "doc": "m0-d01-program-targets.md",
      "rule": "Revising a program plan preserves earlier target dates and their author attribution rather than overwriting them."
    },
    {
      "id": "D02-02",
      "doc": "m0-d02-criteria-content.md",
      "rule": "A program references a criteria catalog edition by exact edition identifier, and existing programs and engagements keep the edition they selected; moving to a newer edition is an explicit, attributed remapping."
    },
    {
      "id": "D01-01",
      "doc": "m0-d01-program-targets.md",
      "rule": "A program keeps one identity through its readiness, Type I, and Type II stages; the stages are planned and do not assert that an examination or operating period occurred, and an engagement and its outcome are separate records from the program."
    }
  ],
  "decides": "Target dates are optional and each revision carries author attribution; the plan requires readiness <= Type I as-of <= Type II start <= Type II end when present. Revising the plan appends rather than overwrites earlier target dates and authors, a target date is never promoted to auditor-confirmed by time, display or imported note, and R1, R2 and T1 milestone dates stay undated until an agreed plan exists. A program holds one exact criteria edition id, existing programs keep it, and moving to a newer edition is an explicit attributed SelectProgramCriteriaEdition at the expected revision.",
  "decidesCovers": [
